 "theme": {
  "name": "Capitalism, States and Institutions (political economy)",
  "why": "Question: how do markets, states and social institutions shape each other, and why do they succeed or fail? HIST 202 (state formation in Europe), SOCY 151 (the social theory behind it), PLSC 270 (capitalism's evolution and reform), ECON 252 (finance as an institution) and 14.73 (institutions and evidence in poverty and policy) draw on history, sociology, political science and economics, as Penn requires more than one discipline. 14.75 as the capstone finishes the same question in a development setting. The learner's PLSC 270 and HIST 202 fit; ECON 252 and SOCY 151 are my choices."
 },
